;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: menu2-draw.gc
;; name in dgo: menu2-draw
;; dgos: GAME

;; menu widget draw rung (issue 759, a2), slice 1: the per-frame draw/alloc
;; road for the six-row lobby dropdown list, landed from a fresh scoped
;; redecode of menu2-GAME (allowed_objects ["menu2"], this worktree's own
;; decompiler/config, scratch --proj-path per the standard recipe; the
;; worktree's own out/jakx/fr3/GAME.fr3 is untouched, verified byte-identical
;; before and after). menu2-h.o (game.gd rank 392) and menu2-installs.o
;; (rank 398, issue 699's own quartet/a1 rungs) already declare and spawn the
;; base-menu family this file fills in further; this file's own row sits
;; immediately after menu2-installs.o for the same link-order reason that
;; file's own header documents (menu2-h.o's deftypes must already exist).
;;
;; Landed this slice: menu-clear-strip (the cannot-decompile class, same
;; treatment as base-menu-event-handler before it - no type analysis exists
;; anywhere for this function, so its body is hand-wrapped around the raw
;; register writes the decoder still recovers), base-menu-method-59 on
;; sprite-menu/prim-strip-menu/string-menu/dropdown-item (the per-spawn
;; allocation chain base-menu-init-by-other's own tail unconditionally
;; walks), and dropdown-item's own state-52 install (the per-frame
;; :trans/:post/:exit driver, harvested from anon-functions 41/42/43 of
;; menu2-GAME, already typed :behavior dropdown-item at
;; decompiler/config/jakx/ntsc_v1/anonymous_function_types.jsonc:1710-1712).
;; selection-menu-manager's own state-52 install (anon-function 10) is held;
;; see its own citation below.
;;
;; Every method-59 body below is transcribed close to verbatim from the
;; fresh decode, keeping every SSA temporary's decompiler-assigned name (the
;; self argument alone is renamed a0-0 -> this, matching this file's own
;; defmethod convention). Two classes of decompiler-only notation in the raw
;; disasm output are NOT real GOAL and had to be resolved rather than kept
;; verbatim, both confirmed by direct compilation, not by reading dead text:
;; goal_src/jakx/engine/load/loader.gc's own apparent l.h!/s.d!/ret-value
;; precedent turned out to sit inside that file's own #| |# block comment
;; (lines 3028-4765) and never compiles at all, so it does not establish
;; anything. l.wu and s.w! are real (goal_src/jakx/engine/util/types-h.gc);
;; l.f/s.f!/s.d!/s.q! are real (goal_src/jakx/engine/gfx/foreground/
;; foreground.gc's own citation, same class); l.w/l.b/l.bu/l.hu/s.b!/s.h! did
;; not exist anywhere and are added to types-h.gc by this same rung,
;; alongside the two it already had, rather than a third piecemeal site.
;; Raw offset math needs an int (or float) base per goalc/compiler/
;; compilation/Math.cpp's own get_math_mode - basic/structure/none-typed
;; bases (the overwhelming majority of what the decoder emits) are wrapped
;; (the-as int ...) at the point of use, and a (begin ... TRAILING) block
;; used as a when/if/and/or condition is wrapped (the-as symbol TRAILING)
;; for the same reason one level up (compile_compare's own none exclusion).
;; (call!) and
;; (ret-value ...)/(ret-none) are decompiler bookkeeping with no GOAL
;; backing at all - every (call!) below is rewritten as a direct call
;; through whichever t9-N register the immediately preceding sets already
;; loaded (with args from the a0-N/a1-N/... registers set since), and every
;; (ret-value X)/(ret-none) is rewritten as the bare trailing form X/(none)
;; GOAL itself uses for an implicit return. Three data-label references the
;; decoder could not resolve symbolically (L940, L942, L962) are inlined
;; from the object's own .asm data section (a string literal, a string
;; literal, and a raw color word, respectively - cited at each site below)
;; since a bare L### token has no meaning as GOAL source; this is label
;; resolution, not content invention, and each site names its own
;; evidence.
;;
;; Three local-vars gaps the decoder itself left (a dead store whose target
;; register never made it into the emitted local-vars list, one per
;; sprite-menu/prim-strip-menu/string-menu/dropdown-item's own method-59 and
;; three within the harvested anon-functions) are declared here so the
;; transcription compiles; each is a leftover, unread call-result register
;; the decoder's own reconstruction still assigns before falling out of
;; scope, not a change in behavior.

;; menu-clear-strip: cannot-decompile class, issue 759. No type analysis
;; exists for this function anywhere (menu2.gc:2646-2647's own donor marker:
;; "function has no type analysis. Cannot decompile."; decompiler/config/
;; jakx/all-types.gc:68695's own extern citation records an earlier attempt
;; to type arg0 as prim-strip that only cleared one of four raw stores and
;; was left unfixed as "a net regression here, same as
;; base-menu-event-handler above"). This slice's own scoped redecode still
;; only recovers eight raw MIPS-shaped ops against an untyped arg0, with no
;; defun/local-vars wrapper attempt at all (unlike every other function this
;; file transcribes) - the wrapper below is hand-built around that raw
;; content, typing arg0 as a bare address (int) rather than retyping the
;; extern, matching the "retyping alone is a net regression" caution already
;; on record. Every caller in this file (dropdown-item's own method-59
;; below, and the state-52 :exit/:post handlers) already passes a raw
;; (the-as none (l.wu ...)) value here, so an int-typed address parameter is
;; what every call site already produces.
(defun menu-clear-strip ((a0 int))
  (local-vars (v1 int) (v0 int))
  (s.h! (+ a0 82) 0)
  (set! v1 3)
  (s.w! a0 v1)
  (set! v1 71)
  (s.d! (+ a0 36) v1)
  (set! v1 #x5126b)
  (s.d! (+ a0 28) v1)
  (set! v0 0)
  v0
  )

